  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Punts and headed goals",
  "description": "Two teams on a pitch of about 30 × 25 metres with a goal at each end and a goalkeeper in each goal. Everyone plays with goalkeeping techniques: the ball is passed only by kicking it out of the hands on the volley or half-volley, and received with the hands – in a catch or scooped up against the stomach. The ball must be caught before it can be kicked on. The player with the ball may not run with it, and opponents stay two metres away.\n\nGoals are scored only with headers: a teammate heads a kick straight into the goal. If the ball is dropped or hits the ground, the nearest opponent picks it up and plays on.\n\nVariants: goals may also be scored by punching in a ball that comes through the air. Allow throws as well, which gives more short passes. Best for players about 12 and older. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Scoop the ball: elbows together and the ball in against your stomach."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Drop the ball low and strike it with your laces for a straight kick."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Keep moving so the player with the ball has someone to kick to."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Head with your forehead and aim the header down at the goal."
    }
  ],
